y feel no remorse when  killing them after all these are big  dumb monsters who want to devour you so  it makes sense for you to defend  yourself by killing them our protagonist  Eren holds this exact view at the  beginning of the story as a child he  always dreamt of venturing  beyond the walls that separate the  humans from the Titans and he hated that  these evil Titans prevented him from  exploring and enjoying the outside world  after the fall of Chicago that district  and the death of Aaron's own mother at  the hands of a Titan Aaron's dislike for  the Titans turns into an obsessive  hatred he vows to destroy every single  Titan in order to avenge his mother and  in order to ensure that no one else will  have to suffer at the hands of the  Titans at this point  Aaron's hatred of the Titans is  reminiscent of captain Ahab's hatred for  a whale named Bobby dick Captain Ahab  loses a leg to Moby Dick and after that  he begins obsessing over getting his  revenge on the whale but here is the  problem a whale is just an animal a wild  beast a whale is driven by instinct he  is just looking for food and trying to  survive there is no ill intent on the  part of the whale towards the captain  and because of this it is impossible to  get revenge on an animal an animal isn't  out there plotting to deliberately hurt  humans if it hurts humans it is because  it was in the process of following its  natural urges and the humans somehow got  in the way in the same vein in most  cases an animal cannot fully understand  that what it did in the past was wrong  so the idea of exacting revenge on an  animal will always be a fruitless  endeavor and the same appears to be the  case with Titans at least in the  beginning Titans are mindless creatures  following their natural urges and  instinct nothing more they don't have  any ill intent or malice they just are  the way they are it is impossible to  exact any form of meaningful revenge on  a Titan you can try to kill all of them  so they can't hurt anyone else in the  future but you can't make a Titan  understand the consequences of their  actions in the same way that you could  make a human understand this is what  makes the Titan such excellent and  horrifying villains they are a force of  nature as unflinching unthinking and  inescapable as a hurricane you cannot  reason with them you cannot relate to  them all you can do is fear them and  their hunger however as the story goes  on we find out that humans can actually  turn into Titans we first realize this  when aaron is about to be eaten by a  Titan but instead he himself turns into  a Titan and proceeds to kill a bunch of  other tight  in his own Titan form now on the one  hand it is cool that Aaron can become a  Titan and use a Titans immense power to  fight against other Titans but on the  other hand it is extremely difficult for  Aaron to understand why he can turn into  a monster how can he  the person who swore to kill all the  Titans actually be one himself this very  concept that humans can become Titans is  a huge game changer but because Aaron  can turn back into a human after he  becomes a Titan the other Titans who  can't are still seen as mindless  monsters our first indication that  something is off even with the mindless  Titans is the 34th expedition and a  Titan that was encountered by Ilse Lang  gnar during that expedition not only  does this Titan not eat Elsa and when  they come across each other but this  Titan is shown speaking too ill say and  even bowing to her and showing respect  shocked that the Titan can speak Ilsa  tries to question it about its motives  the Titan becomes uncomfortable and  starts facing an internal struggle of  some kind  eventually Ilsa tries to run away but  the talking Titan grabs her and kills  her in the process  however the Titan instantly feels  remorse and cries this is the first  indication that we get that even the  mindless Titans have human abilities  like speech and emotions like reverence  and regret of course we later learned  that all the mindless Titans were once  human beings and that they were all  turned into Titans against their own  will the talking Titan who killed Ilsa  is a former member of the cult that  followed Amir from the 104th Training  Corps when she was being worshiped as  the reincarnation of Emir fritz in this  talking Titan appears to have confused  Ilsa with Amir because of their similar  appearance the thing that struck me the  most about the talking tightened before  I read the manga and before I knew the  truth about the basement was how the  Titans seemed to be struggling against  its own instinct to harm humans and  although it alternately failed to  contain its violent tendencies the  talking Titan clearly did not want to  hurt Ilsa the revelation that all of  these seemingly evil Titan monsters are  actually humans who were turned into  these monsters against their will and  who kill other humans only because  their natural urge and not because of  any malice or ill intent really throws  everything we thought we knew about the  world of attack on Titan for a loop from  this point on the video will contain  manga spoilers beyond the current  episodes of the anime so if you're a  strict anime only proceed with caution  you have been warned  suddenly our heroes from the survey  Corps realized that every time they  killed a Titan thinking that they were  just doing the world a favor by  destroying a monster  they were also killing an innocent human  being in the process of course the  Titans were often killed in pure  self-defense and the sea record didn't  have another choice but it was still  such a traumatizing experience for them  to learn that all of these monsters that  they hated and rejoiced in killing were  just innocent people people like  Connie's mother or grisha's first wife  and speaking of britches first wife as a  result of the discoveries found in the  basement  Eren and the others realized that not  only was every Titan once a human being  but in fact Titans are not even the  ultimate villains of the attack on Titan  story it turns out that humanity outside  the walls has not perished and the  humans behind the walls are not the last  remaining humans on earth outside the  walls humanity is thriving and the  humans outside the walls have developed  more advanced technology than the humans  inside the walls including photography  airships advanced military weapons and  so on however the humans beyond the  walls are not living in peace in fact  the basement reveals that the humans  behind the walls are living on a large  island called paradise and that they are  one segment of an ancient nation called  ldiots nearly two thousand years ago an  ancestor of the LD ends called Emir  fritz somehow gained the power of the  nine Titan shifters  and she used that power to form a great  LD an empire that ruled over much of the  world nevertheless the Empire eventually  collapsed because after Amir's death the  nine Titan shifter powers were held by  various LD and noble families and these  families use them to wage wars of  dominance against each other  tired of all the brutal infighting among  the LD and noble families the 145th LDN  king called car  fritzsche decided to abandon the  continent that aldia dominated and he  moved a segment of the Audion to the  island of paradise there he used the  founding Titans power to construct the  three walls and he also used the power  of the founding Titan to erase all the  memories of the outside world from all  the LD ins on the island this way the  145th King isolated himself from all the  war and suffering on the continent and  he threatened the outside world saying  that if anyone interfered with the  affairs of the island he would release  millions of wall Titans and have them  flatten the entire earth after the 145th  King abandoned the continent the LDN  Empire collapsed and the continent was  taken over by the rival nation of Marlay  the marlins now treat the LD ends on the  continent as subhumans and they oppress  and abused them they keep them in  internment zones forced them to wear  armbands that identify them as LD ins  and they use the power that the LD ins  have to turn into Titans as a weapon of  war because they have been using the  power of the Titans to their advantage  the Marlon nation has been able to  subjugate other nations of the world to  its will and while these are the  generally accepted facts the truth about  the LDN empire is drastically different  depending on who you ask according to  the marlins emir fritz made a deal with  the devil in order to gain her power and  the LDN empire was oppressive and cruel  ethnically cleansing the globe for  nearly thousands of years before it was  finally overthrown because LD ins are  the only group of people capable of  turning into Titans Marlins consider LD  ins to be children of the devil and the  entire ethnic group is portrayed as  inherently evil the LD ins are treated  as demonic people who must be punished  for their original sin and for the sins  of their ancestors even if the current  LD ends did nothing wrong themselves  this version of history is clearly  designed to make the Marlins look like  the victims and to justify their  terrible treatment of LD ins including  their exploitation of LD ins for the  purposes of war on the other hand among  the audience who are still living in  Marlay there was a rebel group called  the LD n restorationist s-- and Aaron's  father Grisha was a prominent member of  this group  the restorationist believed that he mere  Fritz's titan powers were a key  from God and that the LDN Empire was  just and benevolent the ancient LD ins  used Titan powers to build roads bridges  and other important infrastructure and  all of this greatly advanced the  progress of humanity rather than seeing  LD ends as inferior in the way that  Marlins do the LD and restorationist see  the audience as superior to other  nations and they believe that LD ins  should once again rule over others the  truth is that both of these drastically  different views of history are very  self-serving and they feed into the idea  that one group is superior to another  where lands believe that they are  superior to the LD ends and that the  audience must be dominated by Marlins  and Aldi and restorationist believe that  they are superior to the Marlins and  that they should rule over them however  the owl  Ehren Kruger an LD and rebel who  infiltrated the upper echelons of the  Marlin military explains to Grisha that  it is likely that both of these  one-sided versions of history are wrong  in Chapter 88 of the manga Ehren Kruger  talks about the power of propaganda and  how anyone can become a God or devil  depending on which version of a story  people believe to be true Kruger says  that there is no such thing as truth in  this world and it is likely that  everything we think we know is actually  propaganda if LD ins were deliberately  ethnically cleansing the world for  almost 2,000 years as the Marlins  claimed then there would be no one left  alive today except for ldiots but at the  same time Kruger points out that he has  never met any human being who is as  completely benevolent and great as the  LDN restorationist claimed that their  ancestor Amir fritz was it is highly  likely that both versions of history  contain elements of fiction exaggeration  and propaganda but if a large group of  people begin to believe all of these  things then in their minds this becomes  the truth and the actual truth no longer  matters this is the same lesson that we  learn from George Orwell's famous book  1984 there is a well-known quote in that  book which states who controls the past  controls the future who controls the  present controls the past this means  that our understanding of history will  inevitably shape our outlook on the  future  and those who have the power in the  present can use that power to manipulate  our understanding of history so for  example Marlins force all ldm children  to learn about how their ancestors were  evil and how they must atone for the  sins of their ancestors by showing  unquestioning loyalty to Marlay they  brainwash the LDN children by feeding  them a very one-sided version of history  that makes Marley look good and aliens  look terrible on the other hand the LDN  restorationist  accused all Marley on official history  of being nothing but manipulative lies  designed to slander ldiots but the LDN  restorationist constructed their own  version of history that puts Ameer Fritz  and the LD ins in an exclusively  positive light and they did this based  on ancient historical documents that  they found documents which talk about  ancient el dia however the LD and  restorationist s-- are actually unable  to read the ancient language that the  documents they found are written in so  they are constructing their version of  history solely based on a few vague  images that they found in these books  they don't actually have concrete  evidence for their version of history  either i completely agree with aaron  Kruger when he says that both versions  of history are clearly self-serving and  are very likely false even if they  contain some kernels of truth and this  is the beauty of attack on Titan and  this is my favorite part of the entire  story the true message of attack on  Titan is that all history is subjective  all history is written by the victors  and human beings have inherent biases  that cloud their judgment furthermore  the greatest enemy of mankind are not  zombies or giant monsters or even modern  weapons the greatest enemy of mankind is  man as hanji points out after the  revelations from the basement the Titans  are not the true enemy the true enemy is  humanity there is a famous phrase in  Latin homo homini lupus' esthe and it  means man is a wolf to man simply put  even though we as humans are so 